1
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:09,000
The Killing of a Sacred Deer is a drama, thriller,
mystery film directed by Yorgos Lanthimos.

2
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Steven Murphy is a renowned cardiovascular surgeon who presides over
a spotless household with his wife and two children.

3
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:15,000
Lurking at the margins of his idyllic suburban existence is Martin, a fatherless teen who
insinuates himself into the doctor's life in gradually unsettling ways.

4
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:18,000
Steven Murphy, played by Colin Farrell.

5
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:21,000
Anna Murphy, played by Nicole Kidman.

6
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:24,000
Martin Lang, played by Barry Keoghan.

7
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:27,000
Kim Murphy, played by Raffey Cassidy.

8
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:30,000
Bob Murphy, played by Sunny Suljic.

9
00:54:27,000 --> 00:54:33,000
Matthew Williams, played by Bill Camp.

10
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
The Killing of a Sacred Deer is a 2017 absurdist psychological horror thriller art film directed and
co-produced by Yorgos Lanthimos, who also co-wrote the screenplay with Efthimis Filippou.

11
01:06:33,000 --> 01:06:39,000
It stars Colin Farrell, Nicole Kidman, Barry Keoghan, Raffey
Cassidy, Sunny Suljic, Alicia Silverstone, and Bill Camp.

12
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:42,000
It follows a cardiac surgeon who introduces his family to a teenage boy with a
connection to his past, after which they mysteriously begin to fall ill.

13
01:18:39,000 --> 01:18:45,000
The film had its world premiere at the 70th Cannes Film Festival on
22 May 2017, where it was awarded Best Screenplay.

14
01:24:42,000 --> 01:24:48,000
It was theatrically released in Ireland and the United
Kingdom on 3 November 2017, by Curzon.

15
01:30:45,000 --> 01:30:51,000
It grossed $10.7 million worldwide and received positive reviews from critics, who praised Lanthimos' direction, the
screenplay, cinematography, and performances of the cast (particularly those of Keoghan, Farrell, and Kidman).

16
01:36:48,000 --> 01:36:54,000
At the 15th Irish Film & Television Awards, the film earned four
nominations, with Keoghan winning Best Supporting Actor.

17
01:42:51,000 --> 01:42:57,000
It was nominated for Best Director, Best Screenwriter, and Best Actor (Farrell) at the 30th European Film Awards,
and for Best Supporting Male (Keoghan) and Best Cinematography at the 33rd Independent Spirit Awards.

18
01:48:54,000 --> 01:49:00,000
The film explores themes of husband wife relationship,
hostage, psychopath, insanity, blackmail.

19
01:54:57,000 --> 01:55:03,000
The tone is lighthearted and dark and emotional.
